A||||18||85ZainoGT||I think I am depressed...||||1||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||12-16-2001||01:19 PM||||I am 17.. Is it possible I could be depressed?  ever since I moved to Indiana in 8th grade from Nevada, its been different, all my life long friends and things are left behind, I mean, I have friends here, good ones at that, but it jus doesnt seem like there is anything for me here..<P>   What can I do to get over this, or get rid of it?   <P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||12-16-2001||01:33 PM||||Sounds like a little displacement. If you are experiencing any of the following, I would really recommend you go talk to a councillor or psychologist:<P>While they may not be indicative of a major depression, they can point to an Anxiety problem associated with depression.<P>1) extreme lethargy. Can't get out of bed.<BR>2) Crying fits. Everything overwhelms you to tears on a constant basis<BR>3) Compulsive worrying. Can't get your problems out of your head.<BR>4) PANIC ATTACKS. These are complicated. Sometimes it can be a sudden and violent headache, and a need to leave whatever situation you are in, to cold-sweats, right up to all the symptoms of a major heart-attack.<BR>5) Inability to sleep. Toss-n-turnin', compulsive worrying...<P>All of these are pretty common of over-stressing. Just a couple of weeks ago, I had a bit of a breakdown. All I needed was something to help me sleep, and 2 days of good rest. Back at it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>NOW, the SERIOUS symptoms that should be looked at right away:<P>1) Total apathy. Not feeling ANYTHING, just vaguely down. Can't laugh, can't cry. NOTHING interests you, nothing can hold your attention.<BR>2) Self Destructive thoughts. Dwelling on what your death would be like, wondering if you ARE better off dead, picturing suicide etc.<BR>3)Suicide. Half-ass attempts, full-fledged attempts. If you can't find help yourself, tell a friend, and get them to go FOR you...<P>Psych 76.101  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000002||85ZainoGT||12-16-2001||01:36 PM||||no, I dont have any of those symptoms, its nothing major, just something thatcomes up every once in a while... i dunno||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||12-16-2001||01:51 PM||||Feel free to PM me, if you don't want to air your laundry here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>First of all, it really does just sound like stress. Unless you are finding things that are really worrying you, you don't need to go see anybody. That's completely your perogative.<P>You moved. Left your friends, your school, everything. You're still a teen, so still doing the hormonal roller-coaster thingy (I am now an intelligent onlooker... Trust me, it's ALMOST over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )All of this will play merry hell on your brain. Do yourself a favor. Try and relax. Do something that you really like. Go out with someone close... Have a good time.<P>If you are having problems sleeping, try going to bed early, and rising at a decent time. Don't over-sleep. Get yourself on a cycle. Bed at 11, up at 8 etc. What you probably need is something not-too-stressful to occupy your mind. Fix the damn car... sit down and actually BEAT one of the bad-ass hard videogames in your collection. Get a job. Whatever. The human mind seems to THRIVE on routine. Moving tends to completely disrupt that, as well as pile up emotional baggage on you as well... Been there, done that. <P>Take it easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000004||TRiAD||12-16-2001||02:02 PM||||I already bought you a car...I thought that woudl help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||12-16-2001||02:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Feel free to PM me, if you don't want to air your laundry here   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>First of all, it really does just sound like stress. <BR>Try and relax. Do something that you really like. Go out with someone close... Have a good time.<BR>What you probably need is something not-too-stressful to occupy your mind. Fix the damn car...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yeah, THAT is always non-stressful <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Might suggest working with a charity or something. Do something to make you feel good about yourself. Meals on wheels or Habitat for Humanity. Good luck Zaino<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||SQL||12-16-2001||02:15 PM||||Go for a ride, I just did and I feel a lot better.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||12-16-2001||02:15 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B> <BR>Yeah, THAT is always non-stressful   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Might suggest working with a charity or something. Do something to make you feel good about yourself. Meals on wheels or Habitat for Humanity. Good luck Zaino</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Are you implying that talking to me is non-stressful?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> Ooohhhhh.... YOU TEXANS!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> :P   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||10
